{title: Good King Wenceslas}
{key: G}
{time: 2/2}

[G]Good King [Em]Wences[G]las looked [D]out
[C]On the [D7]feast of [G]Stephen,
[G]When the [Em]snow lay [G]round a[D]bout,
[C]Deep and [D7]crisp and [G]even.
Brightly shone the [D]moon that [Em]night,
[C]Though the [D7]frost was [G]cruel,
When a [D7]poor man [Em]came in [D]sight,
[G]Gathering winter [Em]fu[C]-[G]el.

[G]"Hither, [Em]page, and [G]stand by [D]me,
[C]If thou [D7]know'st it, [G]telling,
[G]Yonder [Em]peasant, [G]who is [D]he?
[C]Where and [D7]what his [G]dwelling?"
"Sire, he lives a [D]good league [Em]hence,
[C]Under[D7]neath the [G]mountain,
Right a[D7]gainst the [Em]forest [D]fence,
[G]By Saint Agnes' [Em]foun[C]-[G]tain."

[G]"Bring me [Em]flesh and [G]bring me [D]wine,
[C]Bring me [D7]pine logs [G]hither;
[G]Thou and [Em]I will [G]see him [D]dine
[C]When we [D7]bear them [G]thither."
Page and monarch, [D]forth they [Em]went,
[C]Forth they [D7]went to[G]gether,
Through the [D7]rude wind's [Em]wild la[D]ment
[G]And the bitter [Em]weath[C]-[G]er.

[G]"Sire, the [Em]night is [G]darker [D]now,
[C]And the [D7]wind blows [G]stronger;
[G]Fails my [Em]heart, I [G]know not [D]how,
[C]I can [D7]go no [G]longer."
"Mark my footsteps, [D]my good [Em]page,
[C]Tread thou [D7]in them [G]boldly:
Thou shalt [D7]find the [Em]winter's [D]rage
[G]Freeze thy blood less [Em]cold[C]-[G]ly."

[G]In his [Em]master's [G]steps he [D]trod,
[C]Where the [D7]snow lay [G]dinted;
[G]Heat was [Em]in the [G]very [D]sod
[C]Which the [D7]saint had [G]printed.
Therefore, Christian [D]men be [Em]sure,
[C]Wealth or [D7]rank pos[G]sessing,
Ye who [D7]now will [Em]bless the [D]poor
[G]Shall yourselves find [Em]bless[C]-[G]ing.
